module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.DescentDataEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.StackBridge

/-!
# Condition (2) of Stacks 026F from condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI

`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStack` (Stacks 026F) is phrased with covering *sieves* and the *chosen*
pullbacks of a fibred category, while `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStackInGroupoids` (Stacks 02ZI) is
phrased with covering *families* indexed by a type in a universe `w`, together with supplied
genuine fibre products `Vᵢ ×_U Vⱼ` for their overlaps. The implication from the first to the second
is `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStack.isStackInGroupoids`
(`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.StackBridge`). This file builds the *reverse*
implication for condition (2): over a base with fibre products, and at index universe
`max u₁ v₁`, condition (2) of 02ZI gives condition (2) of 026F.

## The two hypotheses, and why neither can be dropped

**Fibre products.** The conditions of 02ZI quantify over a covering family together with *given*
fibre products of its overlaps, so over a base lacking them they say nothing about a covering
sieve. `[CategoryTheory.Limits.HasPullbacks 𝒞]` supplies them; this is the hypothesis the module
docstring of `StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.StackBridge` records as missing.

**The index universe.** Condition (2) of 02ZI at index universe `w` constrains only the covering
families indexed by a type in `Type w`, and *larger `w` is a strictly stronger hypothesis* (a
`Type w`-indexed family reindexes along `ULift` into `Type (max w w')` with the same generated
sieve). The statements below take `w := max u₁ v₁`, which is exactly the universe at which every
covering sieve is generated by a family — `CategoryTheory.Sieve.exists_eq_ofArrows`, and Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.Small.{max u v}` instance for every precoverage says the same thing —
and no smaller universe suffices in general.

## Method

No reduction of covering sieves to a smaller index type is needed, and none is used: a covering
sieve `R` *is* the sieve generated by the family of **all** of its arrows
(`CategoryTheory.Sieve.ofArrows_category`), whose index type `R.arrows.category` lies in
`Type (max u₁ v₁)`. Condition (2) of 02ZI applied to that tautological family, with the chosen
pullbacks as its restrictions and `Limits.pullback` as the overlaps, is the unique-amalgamation
statement for the presheaf `Mor(x, y)` of Stacks 02ZB relative to `R`
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.existsUnique_fiberHom_of_isStackInGroupoids`). Read through Mathlib's
descent API for the pullback pseudofunctor it says that `Pseudofunctor.toDescentData` is fully
faithful on that family, which is Mathlib's `Pseudofunctor.IsPrestackFor`; the passage from there
to the sheaf condition on the double localization `(J.over U)` is Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsPrestack.of_isPrestackFor` together with
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isPrestack_pullbackPseudofunctor_iff`.

## Tagging

Nothing here carries a `@[stacks]` attribute. Stacks 02ZJ is already formalized, as
`CategoryTheory.Functor.stackInGroupoids_tfae`, and its clause (1) is a *sieve-phrased* rendering
of 02ZI rather than `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStackInGroupoids`; the statements below are the
genuinely different implication out of the family-phrased structure, under two extra hypotheses.
They are bridges, and the tag stays with the result that is already proved.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackRestriction`: the chosen pullback of a fibred category, read as
  a `CategoryTheory.Functor.Restriction`.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.fiberHomOfFibreHom`: a morphism of a fibre category from its underlying
  morphism of the total category.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.existsUnique_fiberHom_of_isStackInGroupoids`: unique amalgamation of a
  compatible family of morphisms between chosen pullbacks along a covering family.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.nonempty_fullyFaithful_toDescentData_of_isStackInGroupoids`: the functor
  to descent data relative to a covering family is fully faithful.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.isPrestack_of_isStackInGroupoids`: the pullback pseudofunctor is a
  prestack in Mathlib's sense.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.isMorSheaf_of_isStackInGroupoids`: condition (2) of Stacks 026F.

## References

* [Stacks 02ZJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02ZJ)
* [Stacks 026F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/026F)
* [Stacks 02ZI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02ZI)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace CategoryTheory

open Limits Opposite

universe w v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂

namespace Functor

attribute [local implicit_reducible] Fiber Fiber.fiberInclusion

variable {𝒞 : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} 𝒞] {𝒳 : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} 𝒳]
variable {p : 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒞} [p.IsFibered]

/-! ### Reading the chosen pullbacks as restrictions

`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStackInGroupoids` is phrased with `CategoryTheory.Functor.Restriction`s,
i.e. with *arbitrary* cartesian lifts, while `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStack` is phrased with the
chosen pullbacks. The conditions of 02ZI quantify over the restrictions, so to apply them to the
chosen pullbacks one only has to exhibit the latter as restrictions, which is the content of this
section. The forward bridge needs the comparison `CategoryTheory.Functor.Restriction.fiberIso` in
the other direction; here the comparison is an identity and is never formed. -/

omit [p.IsFibered] in
/-- A morphism of the fibre over `U` from a morphism of the total category lying over the identity
of `U`. This is `CategoryTheory.Functor.fibreHomMk` with its endpoints the given objects of the
fibre rather than `CategoryTheory.Functor.Fiber.mk` of their structure equalities, so that it may
be compared with the chosen pullbacks without an `eta` step. -/
def fiberHomOfFibreHom {U : 𝒞} {x y : p.Fiber U} {g : x.1 ⟶ y.1}
    (hg : FibreHom p x.1 y.1 x.2 y.2 g) : x ⟶ y :=
  ⟨g, by
    have : p.IsHomLift (eqToHom x.2 ≫ eqToHom y.2.symm) g := hg
    refine IsHomLift.of_fac' p (𝟙 U) g x.2 y.2 ?_
    simpa using IsHomLift.fac' p (eqToHom x.2 ≫ eqToHom y.2.symm) g⟩

omit [p.IsFibered] in
/-- The underlying morphism of the total category of
`CategoryTheory.Functor.fiberHomOfFibreHom hg` is the morphism `hg` is about. -/
@[simp]
lemma fiberInclusion_map_fiberHomOfFibreHom {U : 𝒞} {x y : p.Fiber U} {g : x.1 ⟶ y.1}
    (hg : FibreHom p x.1 y.1 x.2 y.2 g) :
    Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (fiberHomOfFibreHom hg) = g := rfl

/-- The chosen pullback of `x` along `f`, read as a restriction of `x` along `f`: the chosen
cartesian lift is strongly cartesian over `f`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackRestriction {U : 𝒞} (x : p.Fiber U) {V : 𝒞} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    Restriction p f x.1 x.2 :=
  Restriction.ofCartesian (pullbackFiber p x f).2 x.2 (IsPreFibered.pullbackMap x.2 f)
    inferInstance

/-- The object of `CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackRestriction` is the chosen pullback. -/
@[simp]
lemma pullbackRestriction_pt {U : 𝒞} (x : p.Fiber U) {V : 𝒞} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    (pullbackRestriction x f).pt = (pullbackFiber p x f).1 := rfl

/-- The cartesian morphism of `CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackRestriction` is the chosen cartesian
lift. -/
@[simp]
lemma pullbackRestriction_hom {U : 𝒞} (x : p.Fiber U) {V : 𝒞} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    (pullbackRestriction x f).hom = IsPreFibered.pullbackMap x.2 f := rfl

/-- The canonical comparison of two chosen-pullback restrictions of one object is the contraction
`CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackFiberCompIso'` of the iterated chosen pullback followed by the
chosen cartesian lift: both are morphisms over `g` factoring one chosen lift through the other, and
such a morphism is unique. -/
lemma compTo_pullbackRestriction {U V W : 𝒞} (x : p.Fiber U) (f : V ⟶ U) (g : W ⟶ V)
    {m : W ⟶ U} (hm : m = g ≫ f) :
    Restriction.compTo p g f hm (pullbackRestriction x f) (pullbackRestriction x m) =
      Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (pullbackFiberCompIso' x f g m hm.symm).inv ≫
        IsPreFibered.pullbackMap (pullbackFiber p x f).2 g := by
  refine (Restriction.eq_compTo g f hm (pullbackRestriction x f) (pullbackRestriction x m) _
    ?_ ?_).symm
  · have h0 : p.IsHomLift (𝟙 W ≫ g)
        (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (pullbackFiberCompIso' x f g m hm.symm).inv ≫
          IsPreFibered.pullbackMap (pullbackFiber p x f).2 g) := inferInstance
    exact isHomLift_of_eq h0 (by simp)
  · exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans (pullbackFiberCompIso'_inv_fac x f g m hm.symm)

/-- **The translation of `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsRestrictionOf` for the chosen pullbacks.** The
base change `CategoryTheory.Functor.baseChangeFiberMor` of a morphism between chosen pullbacks is
its canonical restriction, read between the chosen-pullback restrictions. This is the converse
reading of `CategoryTheory.Functor.fiberMor_eq_baseChangeFiberMor`, and it is what lets a
compatible family of morphisms between chosen pullbacks be fed to condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI. -/
lemma isRestrictionOf_pullbackRestriction {Ux Uy V W : 𝒞} {x : p.Fiber Ux} {y : p.Fiber Uy}
    (fx : V ⟶ Ux) (fy : V ⟶ Uy) (g : W ⟶ V) {mx : W ⟶ Ux} {my : W ⟶ Uy}
    (hmx : mx = g ≫ fx) (hmy : my = g ≫ fy)
    (ψ : pullbackFiber p x fx ⟶ pullbackFiber p y fy) :
    IsRestrictionOf p g hmx hmy (pullbackRestriction x fx) (pullbackRestriction y fy)
      (pullbackRestriction x mx) (pullbackRestriction y my)
      (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map ψ)
      (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (baseChangeFiberMor ψ g mx hmx.symm my hmy.symm)) := by
  have hfib : baseChangeFiberMor ψ g mx hmx.symm my hmy.symm ≫
      (pullbackFiberCompIso' y fy g my hmy.symm).inv =
      (pullbackFiberCompIso' x fx g mx hmx.symm).inv ≫ pullbackFiberHom ψ g := by
    simp [baseChangeFiberMor]
  have key : Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (baseChangeFiberMor ψ g mx hmx.symm my hmy.symm) ≫
      (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (pullbackFiberCompIso' y fy g my hmy.symm).inv ≫
        IsPreFibered.pullbackMap (pullbackFiber p y fy).2 g) =
      (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (pullbackFiberCompIso' x fx g mx hmx.symm).inv ≫
        IsPreFibered.pullbackMap (pullbackFiber p x fx).2 g) ≫ Fiber.fiberInclusion.map ψ := by
    rw [← Category.assoc, ← Fiber.fiberInclusion.map_comp, hfib, Fiber.fiberInclusion.map_comp,
      Category.assoc, pullbackFiberHom_fac, Category.assoc]
  change _ ≫ Restriction.compTo p g fy hmy (pullbackRestriction y fy) (pullbackRestriction y my) =
    Restriction.compTo p g fx hmx (pullbackRestriction x fx) (pullbackRestriction x mx) ≫ _
  rwa [compTo_pullbackRestriction, compTo_pullbackRestriction]

/-- A morphism of the fibre over `U` base-changes to a given morphism between the chosen pullbacks
along `f` exactly when the square of chosen cartesian lifts commutes. The chosen lift at `y` is
cartesian, so the square determines the base change. -/
lemma pullbackFiberHom_eq_iff_fac {U V : 𝒞} {x y : p.Fiber U} (f : V ⟶ U) (m : x ⟶ y)
    (ψ : pullbackFiber p x f ⟶ pullbackFiber p y f) :
    pullbackFiberHom m f = ψ ↔
      IsPreFibered.pullbackMap x.2 f ≫ Fiber.fiberInclusion.map m =
        Fiber.fiberInclusion.map ψ ≫ IsPreFibered.pullbackMap y.2 f := by
  constructor
  · rintro rfl
    exact (pullbackFiberHom_fac m f).symm
  · intro hfac
    refine fiber_hom_ext_of_cartesian f (IsPreFibered.pullbackMap y.2 f)
      (IsPreFibered.pullbackMap.IsCartesian _ _) _ _ ?_
    rw [pullbackFiberHom_fac, hfac]

/-! ### Compatibility over an overlap

Condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI asks for a compatible system indexed by a covering *family*, and
compares two of its members only over a *given* fibre product of the two base morphisms. Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.Hom` instead compares them over an arbitrary object with
two morphisms agreeing over the base. The second is formally stronger; the two lemmas below are the
passage from it to the first, which is all that the conditions of 02ZI consume. -/

/-- Two morphisms between chosen pullbacks have the same base change to a common further object as
soon as the square of canonical comparisons
`CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackFiberComparison` commutes. The comparison factors as a contraction
followed by an expansion (`CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackFiberCompIso'_hom_comp_inv`), so this is
an identity of isomorphisms of the fibre over the common object. -/
lemma baseChangeFiberMor_eq_of_comparison {S : 𝒞} {x y : p.Fiber S} {V W Z : 𝒞}
    {fx : V ⟶ S} {fy : W ⟶ S}
    (ψ : pullbackFiber p x fx ⟶ pullbackFiber p y fx)
    (ψ' : pullbackFiber p x fy ⟶ pullbackFiber p y fy)
    (ε : Z ⟶ V) (ε' : Z ⟶ W) {q : Z ⟶ S} (h₁ : ε ≫ fx = q) (h₂ : ε' ≫ fy = q)
    (heq : ε ≫ fx = ε' ≫ fy)
    (hc : pullbackFiberHom ψ ε ≫ (pullbackFiberComparison y ε ε' heq).hom =
      (pullbackFiberComparison x ε ε' heq).hom ≫ pullbackFiberHom ψ' ε') :
    baseChangeFiberMor ψ ε q h₁ q h₁ = baseChangeFiberMor ψ' ε' q h₂ q h₂ := by
  have hcomm2 : pullbackFiberHom ψ ε ≫
      ((pullbackFiberCompIso' y fx ε q h₁).hom ≫ (pullbackFiberCompIso' y fy ε' q h₂).inv) =
      ((pullbackFiberCompIso' x fx ε q h₁).hom ≫ (pullbackFiberCompIso' x fy ε' q h₂).inv) ≫
        pullbackFiberHom ψ' ε' := by
    rwa [pullbackFiberCompIso'_hom_comp_inv p x fx fy ε ε' q h₁ h₂ heq,
      pullbackFiberCompIso'_hom_comp_inv p y fx fy ε ε' q h₁ h₂ heq]
  change (pullbackFiberCompIso' x fx ε q h₁).inv ≫ pullbackFiberHom ψ ε ≫
      (pullbackFiberCompIso' y fx ε q h₁).hom =
    (pullbackFiberCompIso' x fy ε' q h₂).inv ≫ pullbackFiberHom ψ' ε' ≫
      (pullbackFiberCompIso' y fy ε' q h₂).hom
  rw [Iso.inv_comp_eq, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc, ← hcomm2]
  simp

/-- The components of a morphism of the canonical descent data of `x` and `y` relative to a family
have the same base change to any object mapping into two members of the family compatibly over the
base. This is the compatibility condition of
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.Hom`, read through
`CategoryTheory.Functor.baseChangeFiberMor`. -/
lemma baseChangeFiberMor_hom_eq {S : 𝒞} {I : Type w} {X : I → 𝒞} {f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S}
    {x y : p.Fiber S}
    (ξ : ((IsFibered.pullbackPseudofunctor p).toDescentData f).obj x ⟶
      ((IsFibered.pullbackPseudofunctor p).toDescentData f).obj y)
    {i j : I} {Z : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ X i) (ε' : Z ⟶ X j) {q : Z ⟶ S}
    (h₁ : ε ≫ f i = q) (h₂ : ε' ≫ f j = q) :
    baseChangeFiberMor (ξ.hom i) ε q h₁ q h₁ =
      baseChangeFiberMor (ξ.hom j) ε' q h₂ q h₂ := by
  have heq : ε ≫ f i = ε' ≫ f j := by rw [h₁, h₂]
  have hcomm := ξ.comm q ε ε' h₁ h₂
  rw [pullbackPseudofunctor_map_map p ε (ξ.hom i), pullbackPseudofunctor_map_map p ε' (ξ.hom j),
    toDescentData_obj_hom p f y q ε ε' h₁ h₂ heq,
    toDescentData_obj_hom p f x q ε ε' h₁ h₂ heq] at hcomm
  exact baseChangeFiberMor_eq_of_comparison (ξ.hom i) (ξ.hom j) ε ε' h₁ h₂ heq hcomm

/-! ### Condition (2) of Stacks 026F -/

variable {J : GrothendieckTopology 𝒞}

/-- **The gluing statement for the presheaf `Mor(x, y)` of Stacks 02ZB along a covering family,
from condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI.** A family of morphisms `ψ i : (f i)^* x ⟶ (f i)^* y` between
the chosen pullbacks along a covering family, whose base changes to any object mapping compatibly
into two members agree, is the family of base changes of a *unique* morphism `x ⟶ y` of the fibre
over `U`.

Condition (2) of 02ZI is applied with the chosen pullbacks as its restrictions
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackRestriction`) and with `CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback` as the
overlaps, which is where `HasPullbacks` is used; the compatibility it asks for over each overlap is
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isRestrictionOf_pullbackRestriction` for the base change of `ψ i` and, by
the hypothesis, also for that of `ψ j`. That `p` is fibred in groupoids is used only to discharge
the invertibility decorations of 02ZI: every morphism of a fibre is an isomorphism. -/
theorem existsUnique_fiberHom_of_isStackInGroupoids [HasPullbacks 𝒞]
    (h : p.IsStackInGroupoids.{w} J) {S : 𝒞} {I : Type w} {X : I → 𝒞} (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S)
    (hf : Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J S) {x y : p.Fiber S}
    (ψ : ∀ i, pullbackFiber p x (f i) ⟶ pullbackFiber p y (f i))
    (hψ : ∀ (i j : I) {Z : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ X i) (ε' : Z ⟶ X j) (q : Z ⟶ S)
      (h₁ : ε ≫ f i = q) (h₂ : ε' ≫ f j = q),
      baseChangeFiberMor (ψ i) ε q h₁ q h₁ = baseChangeFiberMor (ψ j) ε' q h₂ q h₂) :
    ∃! m : x ⟶ y, ∀ i, pullbackFiberHom m (f i) = ψ i := by
  have hVij : ∀ i j, IsPullback (Limits.pullback.fst (f i) (f j))
      (Limits.pullback.snd (f i) (f j)) (f i) (f j) :=
    fun i j => IsPullback.of_hasPullback (f i) (f j)
  have hsh := h.isom_isSheaf (U := S) x.1 y.1 x.2 y.2 X f hf
    (fun i j => Limits.pullback (f i) (f j))
    (fun i j => Limits.pullback.fst (f i) (f j))
    (fun i j => Limits.pullback.snd (f i) (f j)) hVij
    (fun i => pullbackRestriction x (f i)) (fun i => pullbackRestriction y (f i))
    (fun i j => pullbackRestriction x (Limits.pullback.fst (f i) (f j) ≫ f i))
    (fun i j => pullbackRestriction y (Limits.pullback.fst (f i) (f j) ≫ f i))
  have hiso : ∀ {V : 𝒞} {a b : p.Fiber V} (m : a ⟶ b), IsIso (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map m) := by
    intro V a b m
    have := h.isFiberedInGroupoids.fiber_isGroupoid V
    infer_instance
  obtain ⟨g, ⟨hgfib, hgiso, hgr⟩, huniq⟩ := hsh (fun i => Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (ψ i))
    (fun i => fibreHom_of_fiberHom (ψ i)) (fun i => hiso (ψ i)) (by
      intro i j
      refine ⟨Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (baseChangeFiberMor (ψ i)
        (Limits.pullback.fst (f i) (f j)) _ rfl _ rfl), fibreHom_of_fiberHom _, ?_, ?_⟩
      · exact isRestrictionOf_pullbackRestriction (f i) (f i)
          (Limits.pullback.fst (f i) (f j)) rfl rfl (ψ i)
      · have hbc := hψ i j (Limits.pullback.fst (f i) (f j)) (Limits.pullback.snd (f i) (f j))
          (Limits.pullback.fst (f i) (f j) ≫ f i) rfl (hVij i j).w.symm
        rw [hbc]
        exact isRestrictionOf_pullbackRestriction (f j) (f j)
          (Limits.pullback.snd (f i) (f j)) (hVij i j).w (hVij i j).w (ψ j))
  refine ⟨fiberHomOfFibreHom hgfib, fun i => ?_, fun m' hm' => ?_⟩
  · rw [pullbackFiberHom_eq_iff_fac, fiberInclusion_map_fiberHomOfFibreHom]
    exact hgr i
  · have hinc : Fiber.fiberInclusion.map m' = g := by
      refine huniq _ ⟨fibreHom_of_fiberHom m', ?_, fun i => ?_⟩
      · exact hiso m'
      · exact (pullbackFiberHom_eq_iff_fac (f i) m' (ψ i)).1 (hm' i)
    exact Fiber.fiberInclusion.map_injective
      (hinc.trans (fiberInclusion_map_fiberHomOfFibreHom hgfib).symm)

/-- **Condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI makes descent of morphisms along a covering family fully
faithful.** The functor from the fibre over `U` to the category of descent data relative to a
covering family, in Mathlib's sense, is fully faithful: injectivity and surjectivity of its action
on morphisms are the uniqueness and the existence halves of
`CategoryTheory.Functor.existsUnique_fiberHom_of_isStackInGroupoids`, whose compatibility
hypothesis is supplied by `CategoryTheory.Functor.baseChangeFiberMor_hom_eq`. -/
theorem nonempty_fullyFaithful_toDescentData_of_isStackInGroupoids [HasPullbacks 𝒞]
    (h : p.IsStackInGroupoids.{w} J) {S : 𝒞} {I : Type w} {X : I → 𝒞} (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S)
    (hf : Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J S) :
    Nonempty ((IsFibered.pullbackPseudofunctor p).toDescentData f).FullyFaithful := by
  rw [Functor.FullyFaithful.nonempty_iff_map_bijective]
  intro x y
  have key : ∀ ξ : ((IsFibered.pullbackPseudofunctor p).toDescentData f).obj x ⟶
      ((IsFibered.pullbackPseudofunctor p).toDescentData f).obj y,
      ∃! m : x ⟶ y, ∀ i, pullbackFiberHom m (f i) = ξ.hom i := fun ξ =>
    existsUnique_fiberHom_of_isStackInGroupoids h f hf (fun i => ξ.hom i)
      (fun i j Z ε ε' q h₁ h₂ => baseChangeFiberMor_hom_eq ξ ε ε' h₁ h₂)
  constructor
  · intro m m' hmm
    have h2 : ∀ i, pullbackFiberHom m' (f i) = pullbackFiberHom m (f i) :=
      fun i => (congrArg (fun ξ => Pseudofunctor.DescentData.Hom.hom ξ i) hmm).symm
    exact (key (Functor.map _ m)).unique (fun _ => rfl) h2
  · intro ξ
    obtain ⟨m, hm, -⟩ := key ξ
    exact ⟨m, Pseudofunctor.DescentData.hom_ext hm⟩

/-- **Condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI makes the pullback pseudofunctor a prestack.** Every covering
sieve is the sieve generated by the family of all of its arrows
(`CategoryTheory.Sieve.ofArrows_category`), whose index type lies in `Type (max u₁ v₁)`, so
`CategoryTheory.Functor.nonempty_fullyFaithful_toDescentData_of_isStackInGroupoids` applies to it;
Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsPrestack.of_isPrestackFor` then passes from the covering
sieves of `𝒞` to the sheaf condition on the localized sites. -/
theorem isPrestack_of_isStackInGroupoids [HasPullbacks 𝒞]
    (h : p.IsStackInGroupoids.{max u₁ v₁} J) :
    (IsFibered.pullbackPseudofunctor p).IsPrestack J := by
  refine Pseudofunctor.IsPrestack.of_isPrestackFor (fun S R hR => ?_)
  rw [← Presieve.ofArrows_category R.arrows, Pseudofunctor.isPrestackFor_ofArrows_iff]
  exact nonempty_fullyFaithful_toDescentData_of_isStackInGroupoids h _
    (by rwa [Sieve.ofArrows_category])

/-- **Condition (2) of Stacks 026F from condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI.** Over a base with fibre
products, and at index universe `max u₁ v₁`, the sheaf condition for the `Isom` presheaves relative
to every covering family gives the sheaf condition for the presheaves `Mor(x, y)` of Stacks 02ZB on
the localized sites `𝒞/U`.

Both hypotheses are necessary: without fibre products the conditions of 02ZI say nothing about a
covering sieve, and at a smaller index universe they constrain only the covering families indexed
by a type in that universe, which is a strictly weaker hypothesis. -/
theorem isMorSheaf_of_isStackInGroupoids [HasPullbacks 𝒞]
    (h : p.IsStackInGroupoids.{max u₁ v₁} J) (U : 𝒞) (x y : p.Fiber U) :
    IsMorSheaf p J U x y :=
  (isPrestack_pullbackPseudofunctor_iff p J).1 (isPrestack_of_isStackInGroupoids h) U x y

end Functor

end CategoryTheory

